{"type":"npc","name":"Rotwood","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":165,"temp":0,"max":165,"details":""},"ac":{"value":22,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":"+1 status to all saves vs. primal spells"},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"adjustment":null,"weaknesses":[{"type":"slashing","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"piercing","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"void","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["arboreal","fey"],"details":"Can't speak any language"},"level":{"value":7},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>When an inattentive druid or other primal magic user attempts to awaken a dying tree that is infested with harmful insects and fungi, they can accidentally create a vengeful rotwood. Wracked with pain and filled with fury toward the one who bestowed them with consciousness, a rotwood's first act is typically to attempt to slay their creator. If the rotwood survives this battle, they then turn their attention to others flush with primal magic, such as fey and other plant creatures.</p><p>While primal magic users are their favorite targets, they don't hesitate to kill anyone else who would stand in the way of their destructive rampages. Rotwoods that eliminate all other primal magic sources in the nearby area continue to wander the woods in search of new targets. When they come across corrupted plants, such as husks, or other rotwoods, they might form alliances of convenience. However, these alliances are almost inevitably doomed to end in violence once the plants' mutual adversaries are no more.</p><h2>Dark Dreams</h2><p>When a rotwood has eliminated all their enemies—druids disposed of, fey banished, and villages abandoned and overgrown with weeds—they sink into a dreaming half-slumber in which they relive their acts of vengeance. Tainted by their dark dreams, forests grow twisted and rotten around them. The rotwood only awakens when new explorers dare to enter their woods.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 45/100/180 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (heavy), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Nature, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, death, elongating, energy resistant (vitality, void), sensory (low-light vision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.gpzpAAAJ1Lza2JVl]{Detect Magic}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.9HpwDN4MYQJnW0LG]{Dispel Magic}), spiked, strength, sturdy, tangle shield, throwing, wild, wood</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Johan Hoekstra","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":-1},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-3},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":-3}},"perception":{"details":"detect magic (primal only)","mod":12,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":17,"special":[]},"nature":{"base":15,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":8,"special":[{"label":"in forests","predicate":["terrain:forest"],"base":15}]}},"traits":{"value":["plant"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"rpHYBm2ldBqm8P4M","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/rotwood.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rotwood","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":3,"height":3,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/rotwood.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRota